Description: Universal Linux Package Manager - rootless sandboxed runtime
 ULPM is a lightweight, rootless, zero-daemon, sandboxed application runtime
 for any Linux system. It packages applications into .lpk files - autonomous,
 read-only SquashFS images compressed with Zstandard and runs them via
 Bubblewrap with zero system overhead.
 .
 Features: 100% rootless install, hardened Bubblewrap sandbox with D-Bus
 filtering, Ed25519 cryptographic signatures, ephemeral RAM streaming,
 universal conversion from AppImage/.deb/.tar, GitHub OTA updates, and
 RootFS/distro execution support.

